<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="252" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Control-plane vault: reconcile the BFF-API-ClientSecret / Dataverse-ClientSecret sentinels with the secret-free Worker (found by T242b)</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — follow-on of T242b step 8 (filed 2026-10-05, owner: "File a task to reconcile")</phase>
    <gate>None for the analysis; every live step (app-setting change, vault write) needs owner confirmation</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Credential seeding and Key Vault references on the L2 control plane (auth/security-sensitive; binding never-create / never-delete rules apply).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-sensitive credential lifecycle with binding owner rules and per-environment judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>touches the L2 Worker template and the platform seeding script; live verification in the dev control plane</parallel-reason>
    <tags>auth, provisioning, l2-controlplane, keyvault, secrets</tags>
    <deps></deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    `scripts/provisioning/Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1` seeds the sentinel `pending-oob-population` for
    `BFF-API-ClientSecret` and `Dataverse-ClientSecret` in `sprk-controlplane-{env}-kv` when they are absent, because
    `modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep` (and `modules/controlplane-app-service.bicep` for
    Dataverse-ClientSecret) wire Key Vault references to them. On a secret-free control plane (Worker credential order
    `ManagedIdentityFederated`, `RequireSecretFreeIdentity=true`) those references feed nothing, and the binding rule says
    never create, seed or restore either secret in a secret-free environment. Reconcile the seeding, the references and
    the rule — per environment — without deleting any secret.
  </prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 control plane, Bicep, credential lifecycle). Follow the binding credential rules literally.</role>

  <goal>
    For every control-plane environment, the Worker/Api templates reference `BFF-API-ClientSecret` and
    `Dataverse-ClientSecret` only where a configured credential chain can actually use them, and
    `Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1` never creates either secret (sentinel or real) in an environment whose chain is
    secret-free. Existing secrets are left exactly as they are.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Found 2026-10-05 by T242b step 8 while removing the script's Redis seeding. On dev all three remaining secrets
      already exist, so a run writes nothing (checked with -DryRun). The Worker template still references
      `BFF-API-ClientSecret` (lines ~120-121, ~283, ~303, ~366, ~420: EnvVarValues / SolutionImport legacy prong 3) and
      `Dataverse-ClientSecret` (the "dummy KV binding" kept per platform-controlplane.bicep's dataverseClientSecretName
      note, pending C1.4). Worker tests `WorkerSecretFreeBootTests` cover the secret-free boot contract (A44.5).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>scripts/provisioning/Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-app-service.bicep</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/platform-controlplane.bicep (+ .json) and parameters/platform-controlplane-dev.bicepparam</file>
      <file>scripts/canonical-secret-catalog/manifest.yaml (never-delete pair)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/Dispatch/WorkerSecretFreeBootTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md (§KV credential lifecycle — BINDING)</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md (A4, E-3)</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner — binding credential rules">Never create, seed or restore `BFF-API-ClientSecret` (either casing) or `Dataverse-ClientSecret` in a secret-free environment. Never delete `Dataverse-ClientSecret` before 2026-11-23. Never purge soft-deleted rollback copies. Never delete any Key Vault secret in this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="live-action rule (owner)">Ask the owner before each live step (deploying the control-plane template, any app-setting change, any vault write).</constraint>
    <constraint source="no outage">A Key Vault reference may be removed from an app only when the app's configured credential chain does not read that setting in that environment — prove it from the code path and the Worker boot tests, not by assumption.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>An environment still runs a credential chain that needs one of these secrets → STOP and present the options (keep the reference, migrate the chain first) to the owner.</trigger>
    <trigger>Removing a reference would require deleting or changing a secret → STOP; this task never touches secrets.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read-only: per control-plane environment (only dev exists today), list the Worker and Api credential chains and which settings each reads; show which Key Vault references are dead.</step>
    <step order="2">Propose the change to the owner: template references to drop (conditional on the chain), and the seeding rule (`Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1` skips both secrets where the chain is secret-free, or stops seeding them entirely).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement in the repo with tests (Worker boot tests for the secret-free chain; script -DryRun); build bicep + regenerate the .json.</step>
    <step order="4">Owner OK → deploy the control-plane template to dev; Worker and Api /healthz 200; boot logs clean.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="file-modified">Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1, controlplane worker/api modules, platform-controlplane.bicep/.json, tests, docs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`Seed-PlatformKeyVault.ps1 -DryRun` against a secret-free environment plans no create for `BFF-API-ClientSecret` or `Dataverse-ClientSecret`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No control-plane app setting holds a Key Vault reference that its configured credential chain does not read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No Key Vault secret was created, changed, deleted or purged by this task.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dev Worker and Api /healthz 200 after the deploy; the ControlPlane test suite passes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Filed 2026-10-05 (session 36) from T242b step 8 at the owner's request ("File a task to reconcile"). Not a prerequisite of T186.
    Added 2026-10-07 (T233 review): the parameter descriptions and comments that call `BFF-API-ClientSecret` the secret of
    "the SAME shared multitenant BFF app-reg … spec.md §9.1 v3 mandates for Model 1" contradict D-13 (one BFF app
    registration per customer). Correct them here, together with the credential they describe:
    `infrastructure/bicep/modules/controlplane-worker-app-service.bicep` (~120, ~280, ~298),
    `infrastructure/bicep/platform-controlplane.bicep` (~164) and the compiled `platform-controlplane.json` (~75, ~1637,
    recompile). Not changed in T233 because the right wording depends on H6/H7's current credential chain, which is this
    task's subject.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>FULL rigor; owner confirmation before every live step.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
